message.content:
Update all value operation nodes (Add, Subtract, Multiply, Divide, GT, LT, EQ, NE, GE, LE, Not, Negate) to accept context instead of %values hash.

Current pattern in nodes like Add.pm:
```perl
method execute($values) {
    my $left_val = $values->{$left_id};
    my $right_val = $values->{$right_id};
    return $left_val + $right_val;
}
```

Change to:
```perl
method execute($context) {
    my $left_val = $context->("node:$left_id");
    my $right_val = $context->("node:$right_id");
    return $left_val + $right_val;
}
```

Files to update:
- lib/Chalk/IR/Node/Add.pm
- lib/Chalk/IR/Node/Subtract.pm
- lib/Chalk/IR/Node/Multiply.pm
- lib/Chalk/IR/Node/Divide.pm
- lib/Chalk/IR/Node/GT.pm
- lib/Chalk/IR/Node/LT.pm
- lib/Chalk/IR/Node/EQ.pm
- lib/Chalk/IR/Node/NE.pm
- lib/Chalk/IR/Node/GE.pm
- lib/Chalk/IR/Node/LE.pm
- lib/Chalk/IR/Node/Not.pm
- lib/Chalk/IR/Node/Negate.pm

Apply the same pattern consistently to all files. For unary ops (Not, Negate), there's only one operand to read from context.

After changes, run tests to verify: `PLENV_VERSION=5.42.0 plenv exec prove t/ir-*.t t/interpreter-*.t`

